From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonid <leonidy.1985@yandex.ru>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:29:57 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: t1100: give the Type-C connector a power opmode

mt6370-tcpc could not probe: tcpci_parse_config() found the connector
child, but tcpm_register_port() returned -EINVAL. With pd-disable set,
tcpm_fw_get_caps() takes the non-PD branch and *requires* a string
property "typec-power-opmode"; without it fwnode_property_read_string()
fails and the whole registration is rejected ("Failed to register tcpci
port", probe -22).

"default" advertises Rp 500 mA, which is what a sink on a plain USB port
should present. With it the port registers: /sys/class/typec/port0 now
reports data_role=[device] power_role=[sink], revision 1.2.

PD itself stays off (pd-disable): mt6771 mtu3 and this connector have no
usb-role-switch/graph endpoints yet, and enabling the PD state machine
before that is wired risks tearing down the RNDIS gadget we use for
console access.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
index 3f42cc84c..f95ee2704 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
@@ -387,6 +387,15 @@ connector {
 				power-role = "sink";
 				data-role = "device";
 				pd-disable;
+				/*
+				 * tcpm_fw_get_caps() only reads this when PD is off,
+				 * but then it *requires* it: without the property
+				 * fwnode_property_read_string() fails and
+				 * tcpm_register_port() returns -EINVAL, which is what
+				 * kept mt6370-tcpc from probing ("Failed to register
+				 * tcpci port"). "default" = Rp 500 mA advertisement.
+				 */
+				typec-power-opmode = "default";
 				op-sink-microwatt = <15000000>;
 
 				sink-pdos = <PDO_FIXED(5000, 3000,
